# Southampton Refine — new thread over junk context

Site memory lives in `site/` files (`QUEUE.txt`, `PROCESS.txt`, place briefs,
`ISSUES.txt`), not in chat history. Accuracy only — no fictional districts.
Coverage commands: `site_handoff.py next` SESSION BRIEF or `site/PROCESS.txt`
§2c — do **not** run `coverage.py --help` (wastes tokens; full parcel model is
in PROCESS / the module docstring).

Build rules are not always loaded. Before surveying, planning or applying any
world edit, read `.cursor/rules/` `frontage-and-evidence`,
`minecraft-craftsmanship`, `geocraft-accuracy`, `radial-good-enough` (and
`terrace-builds` for terraces). Before fetching or viewing reference imagery,
read `reference-token-budget`.

Before doing a new queue item or live-world build in this conversation:

1. If this thread already finished a queue item (lock released / QUEUE marked
   done), or is dominated by prior build/debug, **do not silently continue**.
2. Tell the user briefly that a **new chat** would be wiser, and point them at
   `python3 scripts/site_handoff.py next` (also refreshes `site/HANDOFF.txt`).
3. Only stay in-thread for a short same-item follow-up (e.g. one patrol fix
   right after a build they just asked for here).

When finishing a queue item: after releasing the lock, run
`python3 scripts/site_handoff.py end Q-nnn --summary "…" --view x,y,z[,lx,ly,lz]`
with Shell `required_permissions: ["all"]` (seatbelt sandbox mutes macOS
`say`; `end` exits 3 if sandboxed). Summary opens with one sentence naming
the area and task, then what you did (not an essay). The user must hear
"ready for handoff", see area/task + that short summary, and be moved in
creative to the main change. Do not ask the user to paste long prior-chat
summaries.
